  "explanation": "In modern C++, template class specialization combined with SFINAE (Substitution Failure Is Not An Error) allows developers to create flexible and type-safe class templates that adapt their behavior based on template parameters. This technique enables compile-time selection of class implementations, facilitating generic programming and enabling advanced metaprogramming patterns without runtime overhead.",
  "syntax": "template <typename T, typename Enable = void> class ClassName { /* primary template */ }; \n\n// Specialization enabled when a condition is true\ntemplate <typename T> class ClassName<T, std::enable_if_t<Condition<T>>> { /* specialized template */ };",
  "code_example": [
    "#include <type_traits>",
    "template <typename T, typename Enable = void>",
    "class NumericTraits {",
    "public:",
    "    static constexpr bool is_numeric = false;",
    "};",
    "",
    "// Specialization for integral types using SFINAE",
    "template <typename T>",
    "class NumericTraits<T, std::enable_if_t<std::is_integral_v<T>>> {",
    "public:",
    "    static constexpr bool is_numeric = true;",
    "};",
    "",
    "int main() {",
    "    static_assert(NumericTraits<int>::is_numeric, \"int should be numeric\");",
    "    static_assert(!NumericTraits<double>::is_numeric, \"double should not be numeric\");",
    "    return 0;",
    "}"
  ],
